  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA weak cold front is currently moving across the region early\nthis morning. Patchy low-level clouds and fog are expected to\ndevelop over the next 4 to 6 hours, with high-resolution models\ncontinuing to highlight the area of I-70 as the greatest\npotential for dense fog between 4am and 9am. A Dense Fog\nAdvisory may be issued if visibility drops below a half of mile\nover the next few hours over a portion of the region. Visibility\nis expected to improve after 9am as surface heating increases. \n\nOverall, quiet and dry conditions with above-average\ntemperatures will remain the primary forecast story over the\nnext several days as high pressure dominates. A passing cold\nfront early Friday morning will increase low-level clouds,\nthrough precipitation chances remain low. \n\nThe best potential for widespread rainfall continues to be\nSunday afternoon into Monday morning as a large-scale\ndisturbance develops over the southern Plains and tracks\neastward. The probability of impactful rainfall remains low,\nbelow 30%. However, with significant leaf accumulation on the\nground, clogged storm drains could contribute to isolated issues\nMonday.",
